      "body": "## Purpose\n\nTemporary workaround for a HiSparse P/D race (also addressed by #63827, with a GPU sync): an RDMA (NIXL) transfer into a reused indexer page can overwrite a resident page that an in-flight step still reads, corrupting that request's KV (outputs degenerate into a repeated token).\n\nOnce a P/D request (`do_remote_prefill`) arrives, an unpinned resident page stops being read immediately and its block returns to the pool only after the steps already scheduled have been processed. The same applies to the clean pages of a finished request. HiSparse without P/D is unchanged. Cost: in P/D, decode pages are read from host once written back. Known gap: pages unpinned before the first P/D request keep the old behavior. To be removed once a proper fix lands.\n\n## Test Plan / Results\n\n- `pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_connector.py tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_stats.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py tests/v1/core/test_scheduler.py tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py -k hisparse`: 89 passed.\n- Tiny-model NIXL P/D on B300 (DeepSeek-V3.2 shape from `tests/v1/e2e/general/test_hisparse.py`, random dummy weights, prefill TP1, decode TP2 with HiSparse, 600-block pool, 64 requests per run, 2 seeds). Collapsed = output ends in a repeated token:\n\n  | | normal free-queue order | released pages reused first (repro from #63827) |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | without the fix¹ | 13, 14 | 17, 19 |\n  | this PR | 0, 0 | 0, 0 |\n\n  ¹ main for the right column; for the left, this PR's earlier head where the deferral never turned on (same logic as main). With this PR, 0 NIXL loads landed in a page its owner still read (15-31 per run without the fix).\n- Not yet run: the GLM-5.3 P/D reproduction from #63827.\n\nAI assistance (Claude) was used; I reviewed the change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
